			<ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a113" TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts224" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts225">
				<ANNOTATION_VALUE>This is a paper you wrote Yeah, there's a paper well I remember but the earliest paper I wrote making this point that sharply was a paper called A Comparison of Something and Something Else which I thought was shouldn't literary history of all places it's reprinted in one of my Harvard volumes one of those two Harvard volumes and actually I said he should call it the look no semantics inflection of truth then we would have a good discussion because then one would have included in how can you define truth with no semantic notions at all?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
